Hybrid Mamba prefix caching with a smaller drafter page (backport of vLLM PR #55601, plus the matching scheduler check).

After the KV cache layout is built, EngineCore lowers cache_config.block_size to the smallest prefix-cacheable
group. With heterogeneous pages (patches/../heterogeneous-attn-pages-sm80.patch) a DFlash drafter's attention
group can be smaller than the target/Mamba block -- on a CMP 170HX with vision enabled, 416 against 832. Two
places then use the lowered value where they mean the Mamba checkpoint interval:

1. GPUModelState.add_request seeds the align-mode Mamba state index as
   (num_computed_tokens - 1) // cache_config.block_size, which on a prefix-cache hit indexes the Mamba block
   table in the wrong units: CUDA "illegal memory access" in prepare_attn, or a corrupted resume that loops.
   This is vLLM issue #55600 / PR #55601; the change here is the same.
2. resolve_kv_cache_block_sizes compares each Mamba group with cache_config.block_size, sees 832 != 416 and
   falls back to hashing at the scheduler block (832), which the 416 drafter group cannot divide:
   "Each KV cache group's real block_size must be divisible by hash_block_size". In align mode the Mamba
   group is compared with cache_config.mamba_block_size instead, so the hash unit is the groups' GCD (416).

Written against the repository's vLLM 0.27.1 patch stack; apply after the normal patches.

diff --git a/v1/core/kv_cache_utils.py b/v1/core/kv_cache_utils.py
--- a/v1/core/kv_cache_utils.py
+++ b/v1/core/kv_cache_utils.py
@@ -668,9 +668,13 @@
     # Mamba groups with block_size != cache_config.block_size
     # (mamba_cache_mode != "align") break divisibility; back off to the
     # scheduler block size.
+    # In align mode Mamba checkpoints every mamba_block_size tokens; cache_config.block_size is the
+    # smallest KV group's block (it can be a drafter's smaller page), so compare against the former.
+    mamba_bs = (cache_config.mamba_block_size if cache_config.mamba_cache_mode == "align"
+                and cache_config.mamba_block_size else cache_config.block_size)
     if any(
         isinstance(g.kv_cache_spec, MambaSpec)
-        and g.kv_cache_spec.block_size != cache_config.block_size
+        and g.kv_cache_spec.block_size != mamba_bs
         for g in groups
     ):
         return scheduler_block_size, scheduler_block_size
